doc Function definition: a C function of words.
    Every function takes a first, unused parameter, so that calls can always
    be written `f(0, a, b)` without a trailing comma, then `W p0, W p1, ...`.
    Local variables live in the array `L`. Falling off the end returns 0.
    The `data` section is the function's prototype, so functions can call
    each other in any order.

emit
  static W {name.label}(W _
  {each params}
  , W {it.addr}
  {end}
  ) {
  W L[{frame} / 8 + 1];
  {body}
  return 0;
  }
data
  static W {name.label}(W _
  {each params}
  , W {it.addr}
  {end}
  );
